- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (393, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'Extend ( non-repeatingField )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (393, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'non-repeatingField - any non-repeating field (a field defined to contain only one value), or an expression that returns a reference to one');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (393, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'text, number, date, time, timestamp, container');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (393, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (393, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'Use the Extend function with calculations involving both repeating and non-repeating fields. Without the Extend function, the value in non-repeatingField is used only with the first repetition in the repeating field.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (393, 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Extend(TaxRate) * Quantity * ItemPrice returns 1.197, .6606, and 1.497 when TaxRate contains .06; the repeating field Quantity contains 1, 3, and 5; and the repeating field ItemPrice contains 19.95, 3.67, and 4.99.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (393, 6, 'ref-examplen', 'Example 2', 'Item Count * Extend(if(Company Size > 100; Reduced Price; Price)) returns $1250, $500, and $750 when Reduced Price contains $50; the repeating field Item Count contains 25, 10, and 15; and Company Size is greater than 100. If Company Size is less than 100 and Price contains $100, this calculation returns $2500, $1000, and $1500.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (393, 7, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (394, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'GetRepetition ( repeatingField ; number )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (394, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'repeatingField - any repeating field, or an expression that returns a reference to a repeating field

number - the field repetition number');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (394, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'text, number, date, time, timestamp, container');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (394, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (394, 4, 'notes', 'Notes', '- You can also find the contents of a particular repetition in a repeating field using brackets [ ] as array operators. For example, ParcelBids[2] returns 1200. See Getting the contents of a repetition in a repeating field.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (394, 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'ParcelBids is a field defined to repeat with ten values and contains the values 2500, 1200, and 1500.

GetRepetition ( ParcelBids ; 2 ) returns 1200.

GetRepetition ( If ( IsEmpty ( ParcelBids ) ≠ True ; ParcelBids ; HouseBids ) ; 2 ) returns 1200.

GetRepetition ( ParcelBids ; 5 ) returns nothing.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (394, 6, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Get(CalculationRepetitionNumber) function

- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (395, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'Last ( repeatingField )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (395, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'repeatingField - any repeating field or related field, or an expression that returns a reference to a repeating field or related field');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (395, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'text, number, date, time, timestamp, container');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (395, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (395, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'If repeatingField specifies a repeating field then it returns the last non-blank repetition. If repeatingField specifies a related field, then it returns the last non-blank value in the related set.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (395, 5, 'notes', 'Notes', '- The last related value will depend on the way related records are sorted. If the related records are not sorted, then the Last function returns a value based on the creation order of the records.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (395, 6, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Last(ParcelBids) returns 1500 if ParcelBids is a number field defined to repeat with ten values and contains the values 2500, 1200, and 1500.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (395, 7, 'ref-examplen', 'Example 2', 'Last(Payments::PaymentDate) returns the payment date in the last matching record in the Payments table.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (395, 8, 'ref-examplen', 'Example 3', 'Last(if(IsEmpty(Company);PersonalPhone;WorkPhone)) returns the last non-empty phone number from the repeating field PersonalPhone when the Company field is empty. If the Company field is not empty, the function returns the last non-empty phone number from the repeating field WorkPhone.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (395, 9, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (396, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'FV ( payment ; interestRate ; periods )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (396, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'payment - payment to be made per period

interestRate - interest rate per period

periods - number of periods');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (396, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'number');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (396, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (396, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'Use this function to calculate FV. For example, you can calculate how much you''ll earn on an investment in which you pay $50 a month for 60 months at a 6 percent annual interest rate.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (396, 5, 'notes', 'Notes', '- When interestRate is 0, this function returns the result of payment * periods.

- The FV function doesn''t account for the present value of your investment, and it assumes that payment is made at the end of each period.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (396, 6, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'FV(50;.11/12;5 * 12) returns 3975.90398429....

FV(2000;.12;30) + 5000 * (.12 + 1) ^ 30 returns 632464.97928640....

FV(500;.11/5;60) returns 61141.65130790....');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (396, 7, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (397, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'NPV ( payment ; interestRate )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (397, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'payment - a repeating field containing unequal payment amounts, or an expression that returns a reference to one.

interestRate - interest rate.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (397, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'number');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (397, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (397, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'Use this function to calculate NPV. For example, if someone borrows money from you and pays you back in unequal amounts over a period of several years, you can use the NPV function to calculate the result.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (397, 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'NPV(Loan;.05) returns 156.91277445..., when the repeating field, Loan, contains -2000 (the initial payment), 600, 300, 500, 700, and 400. The result (156.91277445...) is the actual profit in today''s dollars that will be realized from this transaction.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (397, 6, 'ref-examplen', 'Example 2', 'NPV(Amounts;.10) returns 16758.35604870..., when the repeating field, Amounts, contains -5000 (the initial investment), 10,000, 0, 10,000, and 10,000.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (397, 7, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (398, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'PMT ( principal ; interestRate ; term )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (398, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'principal - principal amount.

interestRate - interest rate. If the interest rate is annual, divide the rate by 12.

term - length of time, expressed in number of months.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (398, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'number');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (398, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (398, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'Use this function to calculate PMT.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (398, 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'In the following example, the PMT function calculates payments for purchasing a sports car costing $21,000, at an annual rate of 6.9% over 48 monthly payments.

PMT(21000;.069/12;48) returns the payment amount $501.90.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (398, 6, 'ref-examplen', 'Example 2', 'PMT(Cost;.13;Years) returns a payment amount, based on the purchase value stored in Cost, at a 13 percent rate, over the duration stored in Years.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (398, 7, 'ref-examplen', 'Example 3', '"Your payment will be " & PMT (150000 ; .13/12 ; Months ) & "." returns Your payment will be, followed by the payment amount, based on a total cost of $150,000, at a 13 percent annual percentage rate, over the duration stored in Months.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (398, 8, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (399, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'PV ( payment ; interestRate ; periods )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (399, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'payment - payment amount to be made per period. Type a negative number for money you pay and a positive number for money you receive.

interestRate - interest rate per period.

periods - number of periods (intervals between payments).');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (399, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'number');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (399, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (399, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'Use this function to calculate PV.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (399, 5, 'notes', 'Notes', '- When interestRate is 0, this function returns the result of payment * periods.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (399, 6, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Your cousin borrowed $2,000 from you, offering to pay you back $500 a year for five years, for a total of $2,500 at the end of five years. If inflation was 5 percent annually, with the following entry you could find out what those payments are worth with the PV function.

PV(500;.05;5) returns 2164.73833531....');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (399, 7, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (400, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'Acos ( number )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (400, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'number - any numeric expression or field containing a numeric expression in the range -1 to 1');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (400, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'number');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (400, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '9.0');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (400, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'The arccosine is the angle whose cosine is number. The returned angle is given in radians in the range 0 (zero) to Pi. The input number parameter must be between -1 and 1.

If you want to convert the result from radians to degrees, multiply it by 180/Pi or use the Degrees function.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (400, 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Acos(-0.5) returns 2.0943951.

Acos(-0.5)*180/Pi returns 120.

Degrees(Acos(-0.5)) returns 120.

Acos(2.0)returns ? (not a number).');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (400, 6, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (401, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'Asin ( number )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (401, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'number - any numeric expression or field containing a numeric expression in the range -1 to 1');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (401, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'number');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (401, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '9.0');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (401, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'The arcsine is the angle whose sine is number. The returned angle is given in radians in the range -Pi/2 to Pi/2. The input number parameter must be between -1 and 1.

To express the arcsine in degrees, multiply the result by 180/Pi or use the Degrees function.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (401, 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Asin(-0.5) returns -0.523598776.

Asin(-0.5)*180/Pi returns -30.

Degrees(Asin(-0.5)) returns -30.

Asin(2)returns ? (not a number).');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (401, 6, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Functions reference

