- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (491, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'Get ( DocumentsPath )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (491, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'None');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (491, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'text');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (491, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '8.0');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (491, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'In FileMaker Pro and FileMaker Go, returns the path to the current user''s Documents folder. The path format varies by operating system.

When running on server-side scripts, Get(DocumentsPath) returns the location of the Documents folder. The Documents folder is used as a shared location that scripts from different sessions or other processes on the machine can use to import or export files. See FileMaker Server Help or FileMaker Cloud Help.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (491, 5, 'notes', 'Notes', '-
In FileMaker WebDirect, the FileMaker Data API, and Custom Web Publishing, this function is not supported and returns an empty string.

-
The returned path is in FileMaker format but doesn''t include a path prefix. See About path prefixes.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (491, 6, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'For FileMaker Pro, for a user named John Smith, returns:

/C:/Users/John Smith/Documents/ in Windows

/Macintosh HD/Users/johnsmith/Documents/ in macOS

For FileMaker Server, returns:

/C:/Program Files/FileMaker/FileMaker Server/Data/Documents/ in Windows

/Macintosh HD/Library/FileMaker Server/Data/Documents/ in macOS

For FileMaker Cloud, returns:

/opt/FileMaker/FileMaker Server/Data/Documents/

Each part of the path may vary from these examples, so don''t rely on the path to follow a particular pattern.

For an example script, see Set Variable script step.');
