Returns:

- 0 if the custom layout privileges of the privilege set allow no access to Records via this layout

- 1 if the custom layout privileges of the privilege set allow view only access to Records via this layout. If the database is opened with read-only access, FileMaker Pro returns 1 even if the layout has read-write access privileges

- 2 if the custom layout privileges of the privilege set allow modifiable access to Records via this layout');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (513, 5, 'notes', 'Notes', '- Get(LayoutAccess) returns information about record access privileges defined for only the current layout. It ignores current record access privileges for all other layouts. To fully check access through a layout, consider the return values of Get(LayoutAccess) and the Get(RecordAccess) function.

- See Editing layouts privileges for more details about limiting access through layouts.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (513, 6, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Returns 1 when the layout allows view-only access to records.');
