- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (529, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'Get ( PrinterName )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (529, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'None');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (529, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'text');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (529, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (529, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'In Windows, returns a string with each of these entries separated by a comma:

- the printer name

- the driver name

- the name of the printer port

In macOS, returns a string with these entries separated by the word on:

- the queue name of the printer (if provided)

- the IP address of the printer

If any of this information isn''t available, <Unknown> is inserted in the result (except for queue name in macOS).');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (529, 5, 'notes', 'Notes', '- In FileMaker WebDirect, this function is not supported and returns an empty string.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (529, 6, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Returns HP LaserJet P4015, winspool, Ne03 in Windows.

Returns 24.109.265.43 in macOS.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (529, 7, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (530, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'Get ( QuickFindText )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (530, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'None');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (530, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'text');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (530, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '11.0');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (530, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'Use this function to pass the text that''s in the quick find box to a script when you override the Perform Quick Find command in a custom menu set.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (530, 5, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Performs a quick find using the text entered in the quick find box. If no records are found, returns a custom error message.

Copy

Perform QuickFind [Get ( QuickFindText )]
If [Get ( LastError ) = 0]
    Go to Layout ["Invoice Details" ( Invoices )]
    Go to Record/Request/Page [First]
Else
    Show Custom Dialog ["There are no invoices containing \"" & Get ( QuickFindText ) & "\""]
End If');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (530, 6, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Performing a quick find in Browse mode

- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

- Using operators in formulas');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (531, 0, 'ref-format', 'Format', 'Get ( RecordAccess )');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (531, 1, 'ref-param', 'Parameters', 'None');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (531, 2, 'ref-return', 'Data type returned', 'number');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (531, 3, 'ref-orig', 'Originated in version', '6.0 or earlier');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (531, 4, 'ref-desc', 'Description', 'Returns:

- 0 if the custom record privileges of the privilege set have neither View nor Edit privileges set to yes for the current record

- 1 if the custom record privileges of the privilege set have View set to yes for the current record, or if View is set to limited and the calculation defined for limited access returns a value of true
Note If both View and Edit are set to yes, Get(RecordAccess) returns 2.

- 2 if the custom record privileges of the privilege set have Edit set to yes for the current record, or if Edit is set to limited and the calculation defined for limited access returns a value of true');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (531, 5, 'notes', 'Notes', '- Get(RecordAccess) only returns information about the privileges defined for accessing records. It ignores access privileges assigned through individual layouts. To fully check access to a record, consider the return values of the Get(LayoutAccess) function and Get(RecordAccess).

- See Editing record access privileges for more details about limiting access to records.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (531, 6, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'Returns 1 when the record access is view-only.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (531, 7, 'related', 'Related topics', '- Functions reference

- About formulas

- About functions

- Defining calculation fields

