Related fields are displayed in tablename::fieldname format.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (601, 5, 'notes', 'Notes', '- If FieldNames returns a question mark (?) or the name of only one field, go to the Specify Calculation dialog box and make sure Calculation result is text. Also, you can increase the size of the field on the layout to show more field names.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (601, 6, 'ref-example1', 'Example 1', 'FieldNames ( "Customers" ; "" ) returns a list of all the fields in the default table of the Customers database file.');
INSERT INTO "calc_help_sections" ("help_page_id", "position", "section_key", "heading", "body_text") VALUES (601, 7, 'ref-examplen', 'Example 2', 'FieldNames ( "Customers" ; "Data Entry" ) returns a list of all the fields, including related fields, in the Customers database file that appear on the Data Entry layout.');
